  m_Name: Journal_scan_depth_probe
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  id: journal.scan_depth_probe
  title: "How Deep Is It?"
  author: "Instrument Tech R. Osei"
  dateLine: "Equipment note, Depth Probe"
  category: 2
  body: "The handheld scanner finds a site. The Depth Probe tells you what is under your feet once you are in the pit. Craft it aboard the ship (Tools). It sits on hotbar key 6 by default; drag it to another slot in the inventory if you like.

Aim at the floor you have dug and pulse with LMB, or hold LMB for a live reading. It reports roughly how far below that point the nearest buried object lies, and which way it is offset: ahead, left, behind-right and so on. A ring on the surface marks the spot. It never tells you what the object is: a tablet and a lump of platinum read the same.

The base probe (Mk I) tracks one object and only gives bands: under 10 cm, 10-30 cm, 30-60 cm, or deep. Upgrades, crafted aboard the ship (Upgrades), help. Mk II tracks two objects with a metre reading, and Mk III tracks three, deeper, wider and accurate to a few centimetres. Each tracked object gets its own line and its own coloured ring.

When it says VERY CLOSE, the object is a hand's width down. Put the excavator and burster away and switch to the Ultrasonic Brush (4) or the excavator's Fine focus (3, or T). The Mk IV Holo upgrade, crafted aboard the ship, projects a wire hologram of the scan volume with a blob for each buried object."
  placement: 3
  bodyId: 
  siteIndex: 0
  order: 25
